{
    "schema": "pipeline-strategy-metadata/1",
    "name": "Aviary Lending AMM",
    "description": "Constant-product markets with open LP shares, one side of which, WSOL or USDC, is lent to a fixed Kamino Lend reserve through its cToken instructions while a buffer stays in the market's own vault for swaps. Prices come from the market's total reserves: the other side's vault, and on the lent side the buffer plus the market's cTokens valued at the reserve's stored exchange rate, read after checking the reserve is the one the lent mint lends to, in the layout the program knows. Anyone may call rebalance, which deposits into Kamino or redeems from it to bring the buffer back to its target share of the lent side whenever it leaves its band, and which puts the market into withdraw mode, redeeming everything Kamino can pay and lending nothing, while Kamino's free liquidity is short of five times what the market lends or would lend, until it is back above ten times. The LP fee and all the lending yield go to LPs through the value of their shares, and LPs bear Kamino's losses. The program has no admin. A swap that pays out more of the lent side than the buffer holds redeems the shortfall from Kamino inside the swap. LPs remove liquidity in cash, with the cTokens' part redeemed from Kamino, or in kind, with the cTokens themselves and no Kamino account involved, so they can leave whatever state Kamino is in; and they may lock shares for good in the market's lock account, where they keep earning.",
    "category": "amm",
    "tags": [
        "lending",
        "kamino",
        "cpmm"
    ],
