        {
            "name": "rebalance",
            "label": "Rebalance",
            "kind": "other",
            "description": "Anyone moves the market's buffer back to its target share of the lent side when its share has left its band (the program's BUFFER_TARGET_BPS, BUFFER_MIN_BPS and BUFFER_MAX_BPS, in its IDL): above the band it deposits the surplus into the market's Kamino reserve, below it redeems the shortfall, capped at what Kamino can pay right now. Below WITHDRAW_MODE_ENTER times the larger of what the market lends and what its target would lend, of the reserve's freely available liquidity, it enters withdraw mode and redeems everything Kamino can pay; above WITHDRAW_MODE_EXIT times it leaves and the band applies again. It skips deposits while Kamino blocks cToken deposits, and refuses while either emergency mode is on or the reserve is deprecated. Inside the band, for a move smaller than the lent mint's floor, or with nothing to do in withdraw mode, it fails and changes nothing, so simulate first. It creates no account, and the caller pays only the transaction fee. Inputs are the lent mint and its Kamino reserve, lending market, reserve liquidity supply and collateral mint, which the program checks.",
